      },
      "date": "2026-08-02 19:29:57.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 7:\n\n(10 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. The bigger question is ordering: nothing in master implements check=discard / skip_rx_copy. lst_get_bulk_param() only accepts \"full\" and \"simple\", enum lst_brw_flags has no LST_BRW_CHECK_DISCARD, and there is no LNET_MD_DISCARD or MSG_TRUNC anywhere under lnet/. The implementation lives in change 66536 (\"LU-20342 lnet: support discarding received bulk data\"), which is still open and is not in this change's relation chain, so this one can land on its own. If it does, the man page describes a mode that fails with \"Unknow flag discard\" and an example script that does not run. Should this depend on 66536, or drop the discard sections until that lands? Separately, several of the newly written command descriptions do not match what lst.c accepts - details inline.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 7
    },
